 CellLabel->
  "Out[851]=",ExpressionUUID->"df826437-b399-4557-a85f-7355c02bafbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Meanwhile, the rightmost plot above corresponds to the case of the network ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "773add64-ea82-4a33-9b3d-5a828315350e"],
 ". The links in this network are expected to be a subset of the links that \
exist in the network ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c74be790-ef7f-402c-a720-ae66c37b7c76"],
 " as we have mentioned. Due to the fact that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "46f78213-8fc9-4fb5-bfb4-62b0407c0019"],
 " will have less links in expectation than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ced335dc-1d95-408b-968c-194fa9b75375"],
 ", we would expect equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "4", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0420d16a-dd1f-4bd9-81ee-aa5670a74c69"],
 " to maintain the ordering of links in terms of their dynamical importance \
to an even lesser degree when applied to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2fec235e-804f-4d2b-bc16-b8113f94c430"],
 ". To compound this, network ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "958d0fd9-9db1-4a17-896a-1f3dfa442b6e"],
 " is also assortative, which means that links connected to nodes with a high \
out-degree on one end (which are also expected to have a high in-degree due \
to the symmetry of the probabilities of a link existing in the network ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9d855126-cfb4-4c19-be0c-725d4d33908d"],
 ") will be expected to connect to links with high in-degree on the other. \
The removal of such links will result in large changes to the components of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["u", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5ff50888-90f1-4b5c-bbb5-4a5bb4dcf5cd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "665e2690-f6fe-407e-a1f8-b7fcb5193915"],
 ", which results in equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "4", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d26cbb28-faa8-44dc-b032-882325df9af2"],
 " becoming even more obsolete in this case. Note finally that the \
assortativity of the second type of network being studied is not only \
increasing in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Gamma]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b5bb0c66-0087-4eee-b5bb-02ff5ee1499b"],
 ", but also in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c039082c-16ce-47fa-81bf-26621dd3c637"],
 " (assuming that \[Gamma] is positive; for negative \[Gamma], increasing the \
value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7336e6d3-f984-42b9-a961-d366f8d8119d"],
 " will lead to a reduction in the assortativity of the network being \
generated), since randomness is eliminated and the distances between points \
corresponding to nodes become the sole factors which determine the \
probability of certain links existing for large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "71aab5fa-cf83-419b-9d95-7792f2967f50"],
 ". For such networks with large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d0e73d6b-0826-4aa5-9bf9-f58e57b4c189"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Gamma]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2638825a-c93c-4c34-8751-16c5bb9b6155"],
 ", on the one hand we would expect equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", "4", ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fd50afa3-4fa0-4c36-ad60-8c2e7742b4ec"],
 " to maintain the ordering of links in terms of their dynamical importance \
to a greater extent due to the greater connectedness of the network, but on \
the other hand we might expect a high assortativity reading to counter this \
effect. We will study this with respect to the nodes of the class of networks \
of interest rather than their links in the sixth sub-question of part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fce60d66-635e-41db-b2ee-f22afdbadfc3"],
 " below.\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8194592283693085`*^9, 3.819459240122069*^9}, {
   3.819463789630869*^9, 3.8194637925042562`*^9}, {3.8194638317003536`*^9, 
   3.8194638542627125`*^9}, {3.8194645341287107`*^9, 3.819464743442199*^9}, {
   3.819464909956745*^9, 3.819464958347616*^9}, {3.8194649967751884`*^9, 
   3.819465027397298*^9}, {3.819465076958829*^9, 3.8194654798905*^9}, {
   3.8195437437746024`*^9, 3.8195438068024044`*^9}, {3.81962564850782*^9, 
   3.8196257083118854`*^9}, {3.81962578958649*^9, 3.819625850476633*^9}, {
   3.8196393938629007`*^9, 3.8196394303902044`*^9}, {3.8196394684344807`*^9, 
   3.8196394699723697`*^9}, {3.819639530377776*^9, 3.8196395322627354`*^9}, 
   3.99873680877474*^9},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"bf47013b-4ad2-4f09-8d5a-26c9b016b17e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "        ",
 StyleBox["Node Dynamical Importance",
  FontSize->20,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.5019607843137255, 0., 0.]]
}], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99873592915518*^9, 3.998735951105526*^9}, {
  3.998736801996969*^9, 
  3.9987368067277107`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f402f8f9-c657-6546-b319-\
9f3ff986f577"],

Cell["\<\
I extend the analysis from links to nodes. Each node is disconnected by \
setting its corresponding row and column in the adjacency matrix to zero, and \
its dynamical importance is calculated from the resulting relative change in \
the largest eigenvalue. I then compare the exact values with the theoretical \
approximation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.598452093952716*^9, 3.598452204485716*^9}, {
   3.652420633161273*^9, 3.6524206868278103`*^9}, {3.652420752564468*^9, 
   3.6524207756666994`*^9}, {3.6524208270572195`*^9, 3.652420860190551*^9}, {
