Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that for the assortative networks in SampleF generated above, we now \
observe an obvious exponential relationship between the variable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "in"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "out"]}], ")"}], 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c4091cfe-52f9-45e6-bd50-6fda2ea0bb4b"],
 " and the dynamical importance of the node ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cd859f18-102c-4508-bbba-363243ef24fe"],
 ", which was not apparent in the first plot of this sub-question. This \
exponential relationship is more prominent in the plot above due to the fact \
that the assortativity of the networks is greater in SampleF than in SampleD \
, due to the fact that the parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0f462407-2aa4-40b7-b9af-66e461f5f8db"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Gamma]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a139bf7c-dd1a-44e7-a26e-6fc04b77a397"],
 " are higher in the former. Meanwhile, for the disassortative networks in \
SampleG, we observe very little variability in the dynamical importance of \
nodes as we vary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "in"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "out"]}], ")"}], 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "496ef7cd-c8a7-4937-8c46-be11789e64d6"],
 ", which as referenced above, is due to the fact that nodes with high degree \
will be connected to nodes with low degree and vice versa, which balances the \
dynamical importance of nodes in the network and we tend to a situation in \
which the said dynamical importance is independent of the degree of the \
nodes. Note that nodes in the disassortative network have a higher degree \
than the nodes in the assortative network as we had anticipated in a previous \
sub-question. Finally, note the high variability in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "in"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       SubscriptBox["d", "k"], "out"]}], ")"}], 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "579b4920-46db-4bff-80e9-ec45128ee06c"],
 " for a given value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["I", "k"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "70a3bf9c-b92b-4a57-8358-a3f313d9aef1"],
 " for the assortative network above, which is a result of the relatively low \
number of links in the networks comprising SampleF. As a final observation, \
note that when we retrieve the node with highest dynamical importance in the \
disassortative network ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C2", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "36bcf2bb-bec8-43c8-b7d3-0c2e20950b79"],
 ", we see that its corresponding point in the plane has horizontal \
coordinate close to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["5", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b050d0e5-0c15-47eb-8ffb-8761936c2489"],
 ", while the node with lowest dynamical important in C2 is associated with a \
point in the plane which has a very extreme horizontal coordinate, just as we \
would expect: "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8195302552587447`*^9, 3.819530257677516*^9}, {
  3.8195452693679867`*^9, 3.819545270892366*^9}, {3.819545396258297*^9, 
  3.819545489412465*^9}, {3.8195488485175695`*^9, 3.819549205498586*^9}, {
  3.81954923876643*^9, 3.8195493171346836`*^9}, {3.819549351207639*^9, 
  3.819549522251727*^9}, {3.8195495587497883`*^9, 3.81954958074535*^9}, {
  3.819549754084471*^9, 3.8195499002897778`*^9}, {3.8195500120129433`*^9, 
