   3.8014866716380296`*^9}, {3.801486916405057*^9, 3.801486975596875*^9}, {
   3.801487017370192*^9, 3.801487047063816*^9}, {3.8014871633479366`*^9, 
   3.801487181410654*^9}, {3.801487215713957*^9, 3.80148721859031*^9}, {
   3.8014877143143015`*^9, 3.8014880032888165`*^9}, {3.8014882268073134`*^9, 
   3.8014882413764153`*^9}, {3.8033793583540897`*^9, 
   3.8033794273583603`*^9}, {3.8033796228154287`*^9, 3.803379640089072*^9}, {
   3.8033805615415697`*^9, 3.803380646874024*^9}, {3.803630406717191*^9, 
   3.8036304192536693`*^9}, {3.803630518297773*^9, 3.803630518609902*^9}, {
   3.8036305600929832`*^9, 3.8036305600929832`*^9}, {3.8036307783781133`*^9, 
   3.8036308606011815`*^9}, {3.8053681946307354`*^9, 
   3.8053682120110083`*^9}, {3.8053682718437815`*^9, 
   3.8053683269435396`*^9}, {3.8053683619824047`*^9, 3.805368707126303*^9}, {
   3.80536876819514*^9, 3.8053688654388213`*^9}, {3.805368933520688*^9, 
   3.805368980534671*^9}, {3.8053690139001265`*^9, 3.8053691639045515`*^9}, {
   3.8053692441480365`*^9, 3.80536931864217*^9}, {3.8168635272309895`*^9, 
   3.8168635845935636`*^9}, {3.816863685372053*^9, 3.81686375134494*^9}, {
   3.81686388120994*^9, 3.816863947167095*^9}, {3.816863997606894*^9, 
   3.816864003864453*^9}, {3.8168640429415116`*^9, 3.8168641026916676`*^9}, {
   3.816864152463027*^9, 3.8168641981214075`*^9}, {3.816864244975381*^9, 
   3.816864397479184*^9}, {3.8168661438236933`*^9, 3.8168661720817113`*^9}, {
   3.816866587581563*^9, 3.816866622973196*^9}, 3.8168683686971292`*^9, {
   3.9987362681724167`*^9, 3.998736268858124*^9}, {3.9987364004319687`*^9, 
   3.998736410955204*^9}, {3.998740095003727*^9, 3.9987400973487816`*^9}},
 TextJustification->0.,
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.9, 0.8],ExpressionUUID->"771aa398-3edf-450a-9cf8-77be8b3da462"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In order to construct an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"n", "\[Times]", "n"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9774368-6d5e-428d-89c0-e39e5b9862e5"],
 " square lattice, we introduce the double index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d00a8927-e041-4459-bdf4-f83f056b9bbc"],
 ", where the two indices specified run from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "da486bd6-a0b8-4d9c-b0d1-9bad82596e4c"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a4239314-683a-414f-b5c2-9a34630e259e"],
 " and each index represents a direction in two dimensional space, in order \
to label the nodes of the network in question. Hence, we use the basis \
vectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["e", "^"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}], ")"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c4f7e5ea-f8de-43c1-8ffc-6fd15dccf028"],
 " to construct said network, which we generate using the command below:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.819290842815177*^9, 3.8192908506352873`*^9}, {
  3.819290889815233*^9, 3.819290901862955*^9}, {3.819294317927907*^9, 
  3.8192944447925134`*^9}, {3.8192944926554594`*^9, 3.8192944947528086`*^9}, {
  3.8192945564976463`*^9, 3.8192946776027203`*^9}, {3.8192947199075737`*^9, 
  3.819294746682933*^9}, {3.8192947878587303`*^9, 3.8192948233677263`*^9}, {
  3.81929491530853*^9, 3.819294916260982*^9}, {3.819295010240404*^9, 
  3.819295151052661*^9}, {3.8192952236294827`*^9, 3.8192952591993484`*^9}, {
  3.8192953012887077`*^9, 3.8192953026221347`*^9}, {3.8196275658507204`*^9, 
  3.819627566476009*^9}, {3.8196417539967184`*^9, 3.8196418342211504`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"eb0144fa-f3ae-4030-8595-2966d9f8b015"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", "i_", ",", "j_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"r", "\[Equal]", "i"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{"s", "\[Equal]", "j"}]}], ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", "1", ",", "n"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", "1", ",", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 FontSize->11,
 CellLabel->
  "In[647]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a6181fcf-efca-466f-9610-f5564c5fab54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The command below now connects the node with label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "061fcf9b-9325-4067-879f-06662a6af374"],
 " to all of its neighbours on a two dimensional grid in order to produce an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"m", "\[Times]", "m"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2c2c1d4b-b483-4944-b235-a7600b2e2e37"],
 " square lattice. To see how this works, let us take the case of a node \
labelled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9d44629-9db9-42e6-805a-d385d88e8eca"],
 " for example. This node is on the corner of the two-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"m", "\[Times]", "m"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d1700576-5586-4831-88f5-aaa36f8b45de"],
 " grid in question, and as a result will only give rise to two outgoing \
links to the nodes with labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"m", "-", "1"}], ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"e5d7ca05-a14b-452e-a898-5ddef2cfff93"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", "2"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b29f9141-5a0b-48ff-83b0-dc6e508aba92"],
 ". The command below ensures that corner links such as these and links on \
the edge of the lattice which have three connections are of no concern and \
are represented appropriately since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", "i", ",", "j"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"da222c0f-1220-4d7a-b626-99dade6b4886"],
 " will return a vector of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["m", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f98abdd8-2580-4d0c-92e8-346cfe545d4e"],
 " zeros for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2e294729-c913-4722-81b1-c2e6c3ee85dc"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a5003775-078b-41ba-b7c1-6b3a3657e840"],
 " not on the interval ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "m"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "122f45a2-8b5a-4754-ad76-30e0435d5bcb"],
 ". Specifically, the expression which represents the outgoing links of the \
node labelled ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "953453f4-1099-42ca-b4df-283501152fee"],
 " in the command below given by \n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", 
        RowBox[{"m", "+", "1"}], ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", 
        RowBox[{"m", "-", "1"}], ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"a100ceff-5607-49d0-a171-fed7c4d3e76d"],
 "\n\nwhich will simplify to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", 
        RowBox[{"m", "-", "1"}], ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "1"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", "m", ",", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"174d94f4-7434-4529-b671-c7f100c8f8a7"],
 ". The exact same reasoning can be applied to verify that the nodes on the \
edge of the lattice are properly represented and as a result the command \
below generates the desired network. Note also that the network produced by \
the command below is symmetric."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8192952713956833`*^9, 3.819295320110381*^9}, {
   3.8192958525259137`*^9, 3.8192958747634096`*^9}, {3.8192959145160522`*^9, 
   3.8192959368791885`*^9}, {3.8192959742761326`*^9, 3.819296188433159*^9}, {
   3.8192962246702013`*^9, 3.819296334587119*^9}, {3.819296388331354*^9, 
   3.8192965207839446`*^9}, {3.8192965570399466`*^9, 
   3.8192967613074217`*^9}, {3.819296794997285*^9, 3.8192969244848757`*^9}, {
   3.8192969652557583`*^9, 3.8192969655819225`*^9}, {3.819296996742548*^9, 
   3.819297023575757*^9}, {3.8192971894030476`*^9, 3.819297208409197*^9}, {
   3.8192973132028513`*^9, 3.819297397153221*^9}, {3.8192975770748386`*^9, 
   3.8192975815548773`*^9}, {3.8192976470895386`*^9, 
   3.8192980430941496`*^9}, {3.8192998320077734`*^9, 3.819299876747105*^9}, 
   3.819473503157327*^9, 3.8196418955052395`*^9, {3.8196419343104506`*^9, 
   3.8196419370042458`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"91530479-18cd-4204-aab1-057c9fa83fef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["B", "1"], "[", "m_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{"j", "=", "1"}], "m"], 
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{"k", "=", "1"}], "m"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", 
          RowBox[{"k", "-", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", 
          RowBox[{"k", "+", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", 
          RowBox[{"j", "-", "1"}], ",", "k"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"TensorProduct", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", "j", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"Ev", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m", ",", 
          RowBox[{"j", "+", "1"}], ",", "k"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
     ")"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.817388237746812*^9, 3.817388260417017*^9}, {
  3.8173920194172983`*^9, 3.8173920204296994`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,
 CellLabel->
  "In[811]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ccba86af-15c5-43d2-869b-5287dcc2bac7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The command below now generates a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"20", "\[Times]", "20"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dae28839-407e-4464-bebf-8d30ff994d31"],
 " lattice with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["400", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cc4315e0-d5ee-4e73-8d74-ad83bc54e802"],
 " nodes:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.819298049408293*^9, 3.8192980845283265`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"ab147039-d128-4acc-9f8e-45665af2826b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"B1", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["B", "1"], "[", "20", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.817758017711404*^9, 3.8177580493318954`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,
 CellLabel->
  "In[812]:=",ExpressionUUID->"51cf7b7c-7490-4e08-9e08-b7d29772c718"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We now show that the network in question is bipartite. \[CapitalAlpha] \
graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["G", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b2f5d4c-1e33-431c-be1a-46cdb1fea753"],
 " is bipartite if its nodes can be divided into 2 disjoint sets, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ad76e51d-7efe-4267-a773-d898de9605dd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "24445115-3ed3-47ce-895d-7b3fbb345577"],
 ", such that every link connects a node in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "426f56b8-fc13-4a64-8b28-85abc07b337e"],
 " to one in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e519f224-c8e5-48fb-a356-6683a670ad1f"],
 ". For an undirected network, this is equivalent to saying that the \
adjacency matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "84472f86-8840-4491-a711-8193dc071fc4"],
 " of a bipartite network gives rise to a permutation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["P", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c6fd63ae-ff2f-4df5-a6f2-e63ffbbae7a4"],
 " such that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"A", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"P", "(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
        {"0", "X"},
        {"Y", "0"}
       }], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}], 
     SuperscriptBox["P", "T"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f7113d75-e1d4-49c6-b545-896f475cbdc8"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Y", "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["X", "T"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8999cdcc-6822-4512-b7bc-6339a376d193"],
 " and each row and column of the matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["X", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "01449e59-3d46-4456-875e-af63dcf8a5a3"],
 " has at least one non-zero entry. We now construct such a permutation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["P", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1311f9ce-191f-405d-95d1-b870d3ca589d"],
 " for the adjacency matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["B1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dcb44eb1-3fa8-41d3-973e-7192bd8ed161"],
 ". Firstly, we define the set of basis vectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["e", "^"], "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cb133ac8-78ed-4eb4-8ddc-d7448ecd5dbb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8180201165754137`*^9, 3.8180201223370667`*^9}, 
   3.8181035912816563`*^9, {3.819298117719494*^9, 3.8192981694959636`*^9}, {
   3.8192982189277077`*^9, 3.819298220239232*^9}, {3.819298307544612*^9, 
   3.8192983085549088`*^9}, {3.819298593024842*^9, 3.819298852293133*^9}, {
   3.8192996585678034`*^9, 3.819299676466914*^9}, {3.819299806242704*^9, 
   3.8192998226907387`*^9}, 3.8192998854956656`*^9, {3.81929994530567*^9, 
   3.819299956454814*^9}, {3.819300111991706*^9, 3.8193001312441597`*^9}, {
   3.8193003042054377`*^9, 3.819300313345944*^9}, {3.8193005073309665`*^9, 
   3.8193006063669653`*^9}, {3.8193032091676683`*^9, 3.8193032140246735`*^9}, 
   3.8193110011681085`*^9, 3.8196419688381023`*^9},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"f2cfb6a7-2793-4cc0-9c96-25eedb07c070"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Eva", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", "i_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"r", "\[Equal]", "i"}], " ", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", "1", ",", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8180216001914425`*^9, 3.818021626366045*^9}, {
  3.818029016692274*^9, 3.8180290168079634`*^9}},
 FontSize->11,
 CellLabel->
  "In[651]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cf7150c1-de26-434b-840f-555c4a5f888b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now, the first of the two disjoint sets that make up the bipartite square \
lattice, which we call ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d5873608-1a20-4746-b447-89c290fa2651"],
 " without loss of generality, consists of all nodes which have label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "da72e53e-d8b8-482f-a95e-3338d8a860f7"],
 " such that the sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "22bf465b-431f-4196-bc98-076e91f55939"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "066f19b8-1663-4ec8-8762-0f53e8f13ebb"],
 " is even, while the second disjoint set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e92d5e49-57bd-4666-915e-3d1ee18a8543"],
 " consists of all nodes which have label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"i", ",", "j"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7c00c450-ce3e-4d90-860f-be36fd84ad5b"],
 " such that the sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b53fe962-0b47-459b-baff-0171707ea250"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e8805926-9fb1-4d88-9e9f-c59756b3b8ce"],
 " is odd. Graphically, this means that we can capture all of the points in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "649fb961-fa5e-42f4-bb50-7082f71ffab9"],
 " by starting from any corner of the lattice and drawing a line through \
every second diagonal, where the two corner nodes captured by this process \
are also contained in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a5a3fc36-82d6-42c8-a7f2-6905c5b34459"],
 ". This will yield ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["200", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "41e878c9-6147-41b4-a85b-39835eaf028a"],
 " nodes which make up the set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f0df823d-8187-46cb-8167-5b5e00f8cd3a"],
 ", while the remaining ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["200", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1c9f899f-571b-4f79-a5d1-c044b8892db2"],
 " nodes will comprise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5f631e88-6ed8-45da-bf86-583acc388d58"],
 ". Now, we use the functions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "24d35d2c-7db4-4daa-b85a-b4536e62204c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a3b3c205-3fb8-412a-baac-ba1b0f6830cc"],
 " below to generate a permutation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"P", "=", 
    RowBox[{"U", "+", "V"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e911f01a-b6e0-4700-8c24-2e625a9323f8"],
 " such that the matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"P", ".", "B1", ".", 
    SuperscriptBox["P", "T"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6e0b3a4b-ca63-419d-ae29-b03717476ac4"],
 " will have its first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["200", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "92520539-e769-4573-84ec-c4f968ba6a33"],
 " rows and columns corresponding to the elements of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["U", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1fbeb088-7dba-4ae7-8d78-544c28a47b57"],
 ", with the last ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["200", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d6ad0d6d-da5c-4f93-a7a4-6a218c84264b"],
 " rows and columns corresponding to elements of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["V", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "91aad4ca-a20a-4b1e-b8bc-afd6489e751d"],
 ". Specifically, the first row and column of the matrix in question will \
correspond to the node with label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "73a1d0be-46bc-42dc-8039-be6ee4704e94"],
 " while the next three will correspond to the nodes with labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "1"}], ")"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ca75baa9-400c-47ec-a132-258f1c30c7be"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2f914e7c-75e5-4ee3-a643-1fec747da0a4"],
 " respectively and so on. Meanwhile, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["201", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "373743ba-f1b0-4816-ae3e-076b361663d2"],
 "st and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["202", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5c95a937-f7d0-47a2-b80a-ac793a8ce60c"],
 "nd row and column of the matrix will correspond to the nodes with labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c44786ee-e836-4c2c-b870-2e8d73a11a05"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a6ffa632-9199-43b3-b74f-83ae8b3e984a"],
 " while the next four rows and columns will correspond to the nodes with \
labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"4", ",", "1"}], ")"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "2"}], ")"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e614d305-9703-4af2-865b-fea6e785933c"],
 " and  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3f128cad-5d52-448c-b9bf-f25c01cf592a"],
 " respectively and so on."
}], "Text",
